      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Keams Canyon’s trading post, founded by Thomas Keam in 1875, remains the area’s main tourist attraction and offers a primitive campground, restaurant, and shopping center.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.cpvacationlady.com/DestinationContents/DestinationGuide/659323/0/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Keams Canyon Trading Post was built in 1894 and sits 13 miles east of the Hopi Indian settlements on First Mesa.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.islands.com/2040512/keams-canyon-arizona-phoenix-underrated-scenic-canyons-historic-ruins-native-american-art/",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Keams Canyon lies within the Hopi Reservation and is surrounded by dramatic red sand gorges and scenic mesas that attract nature lovers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
